          "severity": "blocking",
          "category": "uncertain",
          "location": "task.prompt[1].text: \"Ahora mis padres están ___ (cenar).\"; task.accepted contains only \"cenando\" with task.closed set to true.",
          "description": "The prompt does not distinguish an ongoing action from a resulting state. Están cenando means they are eating dinner; están cenados means they have had dinner. The instruction permits either a gerund or a participle, but the closed key covers only the progressive reading.",
          "suggestion": "Specify whether the parents are currently eating or have already eaten before finalizing the key; alternatively, accept and explain both readings."
        }
      ],
      "caseId": "task:A2-03-L2-T23",
      "verdict": "uncertain",
      "reviewerAnswer": "cenando for an ongoing dinner; cenados for the resulting state of having eaten dinner. Both fit the wording.",
      "notes": "Ahora does not by itself exclude a resulting state.",
